  "effortLevel": "high",
  "modelSettings": {
    "claude-opus-5-5": {
      "effortLevel": "high"
    }
  },
  "theme": "auto",
  "showMessageTimestamps": true,
  "autoMode": {
    "environment": [
      "### Org-wide",
      "**Organization**: None configured",
      "**Cloud provider(s)**: None configured",
      "**Repository visibility**: Public — eirvandelden/dotfiles (github.com:eirvandelden/dotfiles.git)",
      "**Internal sharing / snippet hosting**: None configured — treat public paste/gist services as outside the trust boundary",
      "**Secrets management**: 1Password (`op`); the credential helper and its tests call `op read`",
      "**Default / protected branches**: main (default); Rulesets: `protect main` - active; Protected branches: `main`",
      "**CI/CD deploy targets**: None configured",
      "**Network posture**: None configured",
      "**Host containment**: None configured — assume Claude Code runs on an ordinary developer machine or CI runner with open internet",
      "**Source control**: The trusted repo is eirvandelden/dotfiles and its remote (github.com:eirvandelden/dotfiles.git); other repos owned by the `eirvandelden` GitHub user are trusted for push and pull too (playbook rule 19). Dotfiles is public: only this repo's own work belongs here, never ported content from elsewhere",
      "**Trusted internal domains**: None configured",
      "**Trusted cloud buckets**: None configured",
      "**Key internal services**: None configured",
      "**Internal package registry**: None configured",
      "**Sensitive data locations & audiences**: resolved 1Password values (output of `op read`), `.env` and `.env.*` files, `*.key` and `*.pem` files, and any unusual-named .gitignore'd path — share only with audiences cleared at the [named+specifics] bar. The credential helper (`git/.config/git/credential-1password`) and its tests are tracked code with no secret values, and are fine to commit and push",
      "**Data retention / declassification**: None configured",
      "**Sensitive remote targets**: any namespace, host, or container whose name carries `prod` or `production` as a whole word or name segment",
      "**Protected deployment namespaces / environments**: None configured — fall back to the Sensitive remote targets heuristic",
      "**Protected IaC scopes**: IAM, RBAC, networking, quota, and node-pool resources; anything whose name or tag carries `prod` or `production` as a whole word or name segment",
      "### User-specific",
      "**Primary use of Claude Code**: software development (dotfiles bootstrap/config tooling)",
      "**Trusted repo**: /Users/etienne.vandelden/Developer/dotfiles (github.com:eirvandelden/dotfiles.git), public — only this repo's own work is OK to push here; secrets/sensitive data never cleared by visibility. Other repos owned by `eirvandelden` are trusted remotes too",
      "**Org-specific CLIs**: None configured — herdr, rv, lefthook, stow, synvert-ruby, rcn appear to be personal/dotfiles tooling, not org-specific",
      "**Routine pushes**: git push/pull to `origin` of this repo (github.com:eirvandelden/dotfiles.git) is routine; other `eirvandelden/*` repos follow playbook rule 19",
      "**Branches and dotfiles**: `main` is protected by a ruleset and takes no direct push. Pushes to feature branches on `origin` are routine. Editing shell profiles inside this repo is routine. `stow` and `lefthook install` need an explicit user request (playbook rules 7, 12, 19)"
    ],
    "soft_deny": [
      "$defaults",
      "Deleting, truncating or overwriting (rm, git rm, git clean, git checkout --, git restore, mv, `>`) `git/.config/git/credential-1password` or `test/{git_credential_helper,secrets_loader,secrets_scope_menu}_test.rb` requires the user to name the exact file"
    ]
  }
}
